From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rafael Sales <rafael.sales@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 00:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] usb: support 368b:8d81 (AIC8800D80 under the V2 vendor ID)

Some AIC8800D80 USB dongles enumerate as a69c:5721 (Zero-CD mass
storage) and, after usb_modeswitch ejects the virtual disc, come back
as 368b:8d81 with WiFi and Bluetooth interfaces. 0x368b is the
already-defined USB_VENDOR_ID_AIC_V2, but aicwf_usb_id_table[] only
lists PID 0x8d81 under USB_VENDOR_ID_AIC (0xa69c), so the driver never
probes the device.

Add a USB_DEVICE_AND_INTERFACE_INFO entry for USB_VENDOR_ID_AIC_V2 /
USB_PRODUCT_ID_AIC8800D81, matching the vendor-specific interface like
the sibling entries so the Bluetooth interface is left alone.

aicwf_usb_chipmatch() matches on the PID only, so 0x8d81 already maps
to PRODUCT_ID_AIC8800D81 and the existing aic8800D80 firmware set is
used; no other change is needed.

Tested on a ClockworkPi uConsole (Raspberry Pi CM4, arm64): with this
entry the dongle probes and its wlan interface comes up on 7.1.4; the
full patch series also builds against 7.3.1.

Signed-off-by: Rafael Sales <rafael.sales@gmail.com>
---
 .../drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_usb.c       |    1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_usb.c
+++ b/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_usb.c
@@ -2632,6 +2632,7 @@
     {USB_DEVICE_AND_INTERFACE_INFO(USB_VENDOR_ID_AIC, USB_PRODUCT_ID_AIC8800DE, 0xff, 0xff, 0xff)},
     {USB_DEVICE(USB_VENDOR_ID_AIC, USB_PRODUCT_ID_AIC8800DW)},
     {USB_DEVICE_AND_INTERFACE_INFO(USB_VENDOR_ID_AIC_V2, USB_PRODUCT_ID_AIC8800D81X2, 0xff, 0xff, 0xff)},
+    {USB_DEVICE_AND_INTERFACE_INFO(USB_VENDOR_ID_AIC_V2, USB_PRODUCT_ID_AIC8800D81, 0xff, 0xff, 0xff)},
     {USB_DEVICE(USB_VENDOR_ID_AIC_V2, USB_PRODUCT_ID_AIC8800D89X2)},
     {USB_DEVICE_AND_INTERFACE_INFO(USB_VENDOR_ID_AIC_V2, USB_PRODUCT_ID_AIC8800D80N, 0xff, 0xff, 0xff)},
     {USB_DEVICE_AND_INTERFACE_INFO(USB_VENDOR_ID_AIC_V2, USB_PRODUCT_ID_AIC8800D80LN, 0xff, 0xff, 0xff)},
